entRunTokenEnricher` enricher functions and their integration into single/multi-agent dispatch.\n7. `types/reviewer.go`: new `EnrichSummary` and `EnrichAgentRun` callback fields.\n\n**Specifically evaluate:**\n- Does each new branch (cancellation guard, ProcessError stderr extraction, alt-screen width-clamp, token hydration fallback to transcript) have a direct test exercising it?\n- Are tests behavioral (asserting observable output) or are they implementation-mirror (just verifying internal state)?\n- Are there critical gaps — e.g. process-failure case where stderr is empty, or where Wait returns nil but parser emitted RunError (no double-classify)?\n- Are tests using `t.Parallel()` per the repo's testing conventions (see CLAUDE.md \"Test Parallelization\")?\n- Any flaky risk: timing-based assertions for streaming events, goroutine leaks, etc.?\n\nReport: tests adequate? critical gaps? quality assessment of new tests? Be specific with file:line.","agentId":"ab65ccce8349a8436","agentType":"pr-review-toolkit:pr-test-analyzer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me write up the final analysis.\n\n---\n\n# Test Coverage Analysis — PR #1167 (review: surface agent failures)\n\n## Summary\n\nTest coverage for this PR is **broadly adequate and behavioral**. The tests favor observable outcomes (rendered output, event-stream contents, RunSummary contents) over implementation details. Every major new code path has at least one direct test. All new tests use `t.Parallel()` correctly (with sound exceptions where required by `t.Chdir`/global-var mutation), and 10x race-stress runs pass cleanly. There are a handful of small gaps, but none rise to the level of \"must add before merge\".\n\nConfirmed by running: `go test -timeout 240s -count=10 -race ./cmd/entire/cli/review/ -run 'TestRunMulti_Emits|TestRunMulti_DoesNot|TestRun_Emits|TestRun_DoesNot|TestRunMulti_Enriches'` → ok.\n\n## Coverage Verification by Production Path\n\n| Production path | Test | Adequacy |\n|---|---|---|\n| `run.go` synthetic RunError on Wait failure | `run_test.go:345` `TestRun_EmitsSyntheticRunErrorWhenWaitErrIsNonNil` | adequate |\n| `run.go` cancellation guard (ctx.Err) | `run_test.go:399` `TestRun_DoesNotEmitSyntheticRunErrorOnCancellation` | adequate but partial — see Gap A |\n| `run.go` clean-exit no synthetic | `run_test.go:375` `TestRun_DoesNotEmitSyntheticRunErrorOnCleanExit` | adequate |\n| `run.go` `EnrichSummary` invoked before sink notification | `run_test.go:427` `TestRun_EnrichesSummaryBeforeRunFinished` | adequate |\n| `run_multi.go` per-agent synthetic RunError | `run_multi_test.go:414` `TestRunMulti_EmitsSyntheticRunErrorWhenAgentWaitErrIsNonNil` | adequate; also asserts sibling agent unaffected |\n| `run_multi.go` cancellation no-emit | `run_multi_test.go:455` `TestRunMulti_DoesNotEmitSyntheticRunErrorOnCancellation` | adequate |\n| `run_multi.go` `EnrichSummary` | `run_multi_test.go:385` `TestRunMulti_EnrichesSummaryBeforeRunFinished` | adequate |\n| `run_multi.go` `EnrichAgentRun` live emission before sibling finishes | `run_multi_test.go:483` `TestRunMulti_EmitsEnrichedTokensWhenAgentFinishes` | excellent — directly proves the \"don't wait for sibling\" contract via channel-blocked sibling B |\n| `dump.go` ProcessError stderr fenced code block | `dump_test.go:94` `TestDumpSink_FailedAgentWithProcessErrorRendersStderrAsCodeFence` | adequate; asserts fenced block AND absence of inline-jammed format |\n| `dump.go` synthetic-RunError dedupe (sameFailureError, identity) | `dump_test.go:128` `TestDumpSink_DoesNotDoublePrintSyntheticRunErrorMatchingRunErr` | adequate |\n| `dump.go` synthetic-RunError dedupe (wrap via `agentRunFailureError`) | `dump_test.go:155` `TestDumpSink_DoesNotDoublePrintRunErrorWrappedByRunErr` | adequate — exercises both legs of `errors.Is(a,b) || errors.Is(b,a)` |\n| `tui_model.go` failed-agent preview shows error | `tui_model_test.go:121` `TestTUIModel_DashboardShowsErrorPreviewForFailedAgent` | adequate |\n| `tui_model.go` ProcessError stderr-line stripping | `tui_model_test.go:136` `TestTUIModel_DashboardErrorPreviewStripsProcessErrorWrapper` | adequate — also asserts wrapper noise is absent |\n| `tui_model.go` non-ProcessError fallback | `tui_model_test.go:164` `TestTUIModel_DashboardErrorPreviewFallsBackToErrStringForNonProcessError` | adequate |\n| `tui_model.go` preview yields to AssistantText when not failed | `tui_model_test.go:178` `TestTUIModel_DashboardErrorPreviewYieldsToAssistantTextBeforeFailure` | good — guards against over-eager preview replacement |\n| `tui_model.go` alt-screen always-on | `tui_model_test.go:284` `TestTUIModel_DashboardUsesAltScreen` + updated `TestTUIModel_KeyEsc_ExitsDrillIn` | adequate |\n| `tui_model.go` tick/spinner stop after finish | `tui_model_test.go:293` `TestTUIModel_FinishedStopsTickRedraws` | adequate — checks both `tickMsg` and `spinner.TickMsg` return nil cmd |\n| `tui_model.go` runFinishedMsg syncs tokens | `tui_model_test.go:614` `TestTUIModel_RunFinishedMsg_SyncsTokensFromSummary` | adequate |\n| `tui_model.go` runFinishedMsg syncs err | `tui_model_test.go:634` `TestTUIModel_RunFinishedMsg_SyncsErrorFromSummary` | adequate |\n| `tui_model.go` cached termWidth used before resize msg | `tui_model_test.go:499` `TestTUIModel_DashboardUsesCachedTerminalWidthBeforeResizeMsg` | adequate |\n| `manifest.go` hydrate from session-state TokenUsage | `manifest_test.go:24` `TestHydrateReviewSummaryTokensFromStates_PopulatesTokensFromSessionState` | adequate — covers cache-creation/read addition + subagent recursion |\n| `manifest.go` hydrate falls back to transcript | `manifest_test.go:61` `TestHydrateReviewSummaryTokensFromStates_FallsBackToTranscript` | adequate; correctly uses `t.Cleanup` to restore `reviewAgentByType` |\n| `cmd.go` enrichers wire to current session state | `manifest_test.go:108` `TestReviewSummaryTokenEnricher_LoadsCurrentSessionState` | adequate (integration-y) |\n| `types/reviewer.go` `EnrichSummary` / `EnrichAgentRun` fields | covered by the run/run_multi enricher tests above | adequate |\n| `tui_sink.go` `terminalMeasurer` + width pre-Program | not covered | **Gap B** |\n\n## Critical Gaps\n\nNone rated 8+. The PR is mergeable from a coverage standpoint.\n\n## Important Improvements (rated 5–7)\n\n**Gap A — Per-process timeout / deadline without outer-ctx cancel (rating 6)**\nLocation: `cmd/entire/cli/review/run.go:127-131` (`shouldEmitSyntheticRunError`).\nThe second guard branch (`errors.Is(waitErr, context.Canceled) || errors.Is(waitErr, context.DeadlineExceeded)`) is dead-coded by the current cancellation test. `TestRun_DoesNotEmitSyntheticRunErrorOnCancellation` (`run_test.go:399`) sets BOTH the outer ctx cancelled AND `waitErr=context.Canceled`, so it short-circuits in the `ctx.Err() != nil` branch first. A real scenario this guard exists for: an agent process times out via an internal `context.WithTimeout` while the outer review ctx is still alive (e.g., a per-agent deadline in a future reviewer impl). Suggested test: outer ctx alive, `stubReviewer.waitErr=context.DeadlineExceeded`, assert no synthetic RunError event in `rec.agentEvents`.\n\n**Gap B — `terminalMeasurer` width/height pre-Program (rating 6)**\nLocation: `cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_sink.go:77-95`.\nThe new `terminalMeasurer` function and the `model.termWidth/termHeight` pre-seed in `NewTUISink` (`tui_sink.go:59-63`) have no direct test. Existing TUI sink tests use `bytes.Buffer` which does NOT implement `Fd()`, so they only exercise the `return nil` branch. Concrete failure this would catch: a refactor that drops the pre-Program measurement, breaking the user-visible behavior where the first frame is clamped to the actual terminal width before the first `WindowSizeMsg` arrives. Suggested test: pass a fake `fdWriter` with a controllable `Fd()` value, or refactor `terminalMeasurer` to accept a `func(fd) (w,h,err)` parameter and inject a stub.\n\n**Gap C — `ProcessError{Stderr: \"\"}` (rating 5)**\nLocation: `cmd/entire/cli/review/dump.go:107-112` and `cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go:439-451`.\nBoth `writeFailureHeader` and `formatErrorPreview` have a `ProcessError`-with-empty-stderr branch that's currently untested. In `dump.go`, the branch falls through to `\"**Failed:** `%v`\"` which prints `pe.Error()` → `\"claude-code: exit status 1\"`. In `tui_model.go`, `formatErrorPreview` falls through the empty-stderr loop and returns `pe.Err.Error()`. Concrete failure: a future refactor that swallows the fallback in either function would render a bare `**Failed:**` (no exit detail) for any agent that exits non-zero with no stderr — a regression in actionability. Suggested tests:\n- `TestDumpSink_FailedAgentWithProcessErrorEmptyStderrUsesErrorString`\n- `TestTUIModel_DashboardErrorPreviewWithProcessErrorEmptyStderrUsesErrInError`\n\n**Gap D — Enricher returns original summary on store error (rating 5)**\nLocation: `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go:685-707`.\n`reviewSummaryTokenEnricher` and `reviewAgentRunTokenEnricher` both have an explicit \"log debug + return original\" path when `hydrateReviewSummaryTokensFromCurrentState` returns an error (e.g., `NewStateStore` or `List` failure). No test covers this — running with a corrupted state store should not blank out the summary. Suggested test: invoke the enricher with a deliberately broken store (or in a directory where `NewStateStore` errors), assert the returned summary equals the input summary.\n\n**Gap E — `run.go` torn-stream + nil-waitErr: parser RunError must not be duplicated (rating 5)**\nLocation: `cmd/entire/cli/review/run.go:85-95`.\nThe existing `TestRun_TornStreamCleanExitClassifiedAsFailed` (`run_test.go:202`) verifies status & error but does not count how many `RunError` events end up in `summary.AgentRuns[0].Buffer` or in the sink's event stream. Today the behavior is correct (waitErr=nil → no synthetic), but the test doesn't pin that contract. A refactor that drops the `waitErr == nil → return false` guard in `shouldEmitSyntheticRunError` would silently double-classify a torn-stream run. Suggested addition to the existing test: assert exactly ONE `RunError` event in `summary.AgentRuns[0].Buffer` and in the sink-recorded events.\n\n## Test Quality Observations (positives)\n\n- **`TestRunMulti_EmitsEnrichedTokensWhenAgentFinishes`** (`run_multi_test.go:483`) is high-quality: it deliberately blocks agent-B's event channel and verifies agent-A's enriched tokens reach the sink BEFORE the run finishes. This is the right shape of test for a streaming-progress feature — it would catch a refactor that batched enrichment until `RunMulti` returned.\n- **`TestDumpSink_DoesNotDoublePrintRunErrorWrappedByRunErr`** (`dump_test.go:155`) explicitly verifies the `errors.Is(b,a)` reverse-direction branch of `sameFailureError`, which is easy to miss when reading the implementation. Strong test.\n- **`TestTUIModel_DashboardErrorPreviewStripsProcessErrorWrapper`** (`tui_model_test.go:136`) is precise: it asserts both the positive (first stderr line) AND the absence of three specific wrapper strings (`error: codex:`, `exit status 1:`, `stderr:`). This kind of dual assertion is much harder to fool than a single-substring check.\n- **`TestTUIModel_FinishedStopsTickRedraws`** (`tui_model_test.go:293`) asserts the contract via the actual `tea.Cmd` returned — testing behavior at the right level.\n- **`TestHydrateReviewSummaryTokensFromStates_FallsBackToTranscript`** (`manifest_test.go:61`) correctly uses `t.Cleanup` for `reviewAgentByType` restoration, and additionally asserts the test agent does NOT leak into `agent.List()` (`manifest_test.go:103-105`) — defensive testing.\n\n## Test Parallelization Compliance\n\nAll new tests follow the repo's `t.Parallel()` convention.\n- 17/18 new tests call `t.Parallel()`.\n- `TestHydrateReviewSummaryTokensFromStates_FallsBackToTranscript` (`manifest_test.go:61`) omits it because it mutates the `reviewAgentByType` package var — correct exception, parallel-with-other-tests would race.\n- `TestReviewSummaryTokenEnricher_LoadsCurrentSessionState` (`manifest_test.go:108`) omits it because it uses `t.Chdir` — correct exception per CLAUDE.md.\n\n## Flaky Risk Assessment\n\nLow. The streaming test (`TestRunMulti_EmitsEnrichedTokensWhenAgentFinishes`) uses bounded channels with `select`/`time.After(time.Second)` timeouts — 1s is generous for a non-blocking channel send. Race-detector x10 passes. No `sleep`-based assertions. No goroutine leaks (all goroutines are joined via `done` channels or `chanProcess.events`-close).\n\nThe only nit: `liveTokenSink.AgentEvent` (`run_multi_test.go:551-559`) does a blocking send on `s.tokens` (size 1) — if the test ever stopped reading from `sink.tokens`, the orchestrator would block. The current flow reads exactly once before closing `eventsB`, so this is correct, but it's a subtle invariant. Not worth fixing.\n\n## Files Referenced\n\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/run.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/run_multi.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/dump.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_sink.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/run_test.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/run_multi_test.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/dump_test.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model_test.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest_test.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_sink_test.go`\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go`\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Tests are adequate to merge.** The five gaps above are all single-test additions that would strengthen the safety net but don't represent material regression risk today. If I had to prioritize: Gap A (per-process deadline guard) and Gap C (empty-stderr ProcessError) are the most worth adding because they exercise existing-but-untested branches in production code paths the PR specifically claims to handle."}],"totalDurationMs":270260,"totalTokens":139732,"totalToolUseCount":57,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":133488,"output_tokens":6084,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":159},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":6084,"cache_read_input_tokens":133488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":159,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":8,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":49,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bae8c460-f208-4e8c-b3cb-7dba86d9947d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli","sessionId":"e755fa5c-b328-4df6-9d0e-c68b395e061e","version":"2.1.139","gitBranch":"feat/review-manifest-diagnostic"}
{"parentUuid":"948d4c7b-3d93-44d1-8bea-4f5396a224c0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a9614f47-41df-47ed-8947-b9c54a028dad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012QPHBYYiVgokqSuFaUcqxW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note: Single-agent path doesn't set `EnrichAgentRun`, only `EnrichSummary`. Multi-agent path sets both. This is asymmetric. The reason is that single-agent only has one `RunFinished` event so live token updates between agents are irrelevant — but the `EnrichSummary` still hydrates tokens for the final view. Reasonable.\n\nNow let me compile my findings.\n\n---\n\n## PR #1167 Review\n\n**Scope reviewed:** `cmd/entire/cli/review/` package changes for surfacing agent failures and live multi-agent progress, including new `EnrichSummary`/`EnrichAgentRun` callbacks, synthetic `RunError` emission, token hydration, TUI alt-screen/measured-width changes, and dump-sink stderr rendering.\n\n### Critical issues (90-100)\n\nNone — the synthetic-RunError cancellation guard is correct, the close-after-wait protocol is preserved, no anti-features are recreated, logging uses the right helpers, and errors are properly wrapped.\n\n### Important issues (80-89)\n\n**1. `RunConfig` is now overloaded with orchestrator callbacks — leaky abstraction risk** (confidence 82)\n- File: `cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go:105-114`\n- The doc comment on `RunConfig` says \"immutable per-run configuration passed to AgentReviewer.Start\" (line 95-99), but `EnrichSummary`/`EnrichAgentRun` are orchestrator-only callbacks the agent reviewer never inspects. Evidence of the mismatch: `perAgentConfiguredReviewer.Start` (cmd.go:753) ignores its incoming `RunConfig` entirely and substitutes its own `r.cfg`, so per-agent reviewers literally never see the enricher fields even when set.\n- This conflates two distinct concerns: \"what the agent receives\" vs. \"what the orchestrator does with results\". The contract in the doc comment is now misleading.\n- Suggested fix: extract a separate `RunOptions` (or `OrchestrationHooks`) struct and pass it as a third parameter to `Run`/`RunMulti`, or document the split explicitly in `RunConfig`'s doc comment (note that some fields are agent-facing and others are orchestrator-only).\n\n**2. Package-level `reviewAgentByType` var creates a test-parallelism foot-gun** (confidence 80)\n- File: `cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go:23`\n- `TestHydrateReviewSummaryTokensFromStates_FallsBackToTranscript` (manifest_test.go:60) mutates this var without `t.Parallel()`. Other parallel tests in the same file (manifest_test.go:25) call `hydrateReviewSummaryTokensFromStates`, but happen to take the short-circuit path that never reads `reviewAgentByType`. The arrangement is correct today but silently fragile — any future parallel test that triggers the transcript fallback will race.\n- Suggested fix: thread the lookup through the call chain (e.g., add an `agentByType` field to a helper struct or accept it as a function parameter), or accept the global and add a defensive `t.Setenv`-style restore + explicit comment forbidding parallel use when the var is mutated.\n\n### Suggestions / nice-to-have (76-79, included because they're concrete)\n\n**3. `reviewTokenUsageForSession` silently swallows transcript read errors** (confidence 78)\n- File: `cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go:185-192`\n- `os.ReadFile(st.TranscriptPath)` failures and `reviewAgentByType(...)` lookup errors return nil with no log line, so users see \"no tokens\" without any debug breadcrumb. The orchestrator-level enricher wrapper logs the create/list errors but not these inner failures.\n- Suggested fix: add a `logging.Debug(ctx, \"review token transcript read failed\", slog.String(\"path\", st.TranscriptPath), slog.String(\"error\", err.Error()))` on each silent-nil branch so debugging missing tokens doesn't require a debugger.\n\n**4. `EnrichSummary` runs inline on the orchestrator goroutine and does disk I/O** (confidence 76)\n- Files: `cmd/entire/cli/review/run.go:117` and `cmd/entire/cli/review/run_multi.go:223`\n- `enrichRunSummary` is called synchronously before `sink.RunFinished` fires. The enricher calls `session.NewStateStore.List` and `os.ReadFile` per agent. For very large transcripts (token-extraction can be O(MB)), this delays the final dashboard frame visible to the user.\n- Suggested fix: either document the latency contract on `RunConfig.EnrichSummary` (\"may block; runs on the dispatch goroutine after all agents exit\"), or move enrichment behind a timeout / cap transcript read size. Same applies to `emitEnrichedAgentTokens` running in the per-agent goroutine.\n\n### Strengths\n\n- **Synthetic `RunError` cancellation guard is correct.** `shouldEmitSyntheticRunError` (run.go:130-141) checks both `ctx.Err()` and `errors.Is(waitErr, context.Canceled/DeadlineExceeded)`, so a Ctrl+C that produces a non-canonical wait error (e.g., `*exec.ExitError` with `-1`) still gets correctly classified as cancellation rather than misemitted as a synthetic error event. Tests at run_test.go:434 and run_multi_test.go:455 pin this behavior.\n- **Close-after-wait protocol is preserved in `RunMulti`.** The new synthetic `RunError`/`Tokens` sends happen before `wg.Done` in the per-agent goroutine (run_multi.go:140-149), so the dispatch loop sees them via the fan-in channel before `wg.Wait → close(fanIn)` lets the loop exit. The doc comment at run_multi.go:42-44 is updated to reflect this.\n- **`sameFailureError` cross-direction wrapping check is sound.** dump.go:108-113 uses bidirectional `errors.Is` to detect when a buffered `RunError` event is the same failure already reported via `run.Err`, including the `agentRunFailureError` wrap case. Test coverage at dump_test.go:192 confirms the wrapping case is handled.\n- **Anti-features list compliance.** No `PendingReviewMarker`, no `WorktreePath` field on summary structs, no `--track-only`/`--postreview` resurrection, no parallel `si